Converts `SecureBuffer` from a runtime-sized class with raw `new[]/delete[]` to a compile-time-sized class template backed by `std::array<uint8_t, N>`. Resolves merge conflict with the `std::span` API change from #6.

- **`SecureBuffer.hpp`** — Now a header-only template `SecureBuffer<N>` using `std::array<uint8_t, N>` storage. `data()` returns `std::span` (per #6). Eliminates manual memory management entirely.
- **`SecureBuffer.cpp`** — Explicit template instantiations for common buffer sizes (16, 32, 64, 128, 256 bytes)
- **`CMakeLists.txt`** — Unchanged from master (keeps `SecureBuffer.cpp` in sources)

```cpp
// Before
SecureBuffer buf(32);
uint8_t* p = buf.data();

// After
SecureBuffer<32> buf;
std::span<uint8_t> view = buf.data();
```

All security properties preserved: `mlock`/`munlock`, volatile-barrier zeroization, move-only semantics with source zeroization on move.

