Google login was failing with "Invalid authentication token" error. The token verification logic was comparing the `aud` field against `FIREBASE_API_KEY`, but Firebase ID tokens set `aud` to the project ID, not the API key.

## Changes

- **`server/firebase.js:95-105`**: Simplified audience validation to compare `tokenInfo.aud` directly against `this.projectId`
- **`server/firebase.js:79-82`**: Added upfront check that `projectId` is configured before attempting verification

### Before
```javascript
if (tokenInfo.aud !== config.FIREBASE_API_KEY && 
    tokenInfo.azp !== config.FIREBASE_API_KEY) {
    if (!tokenInfo.aud?.includes(this.projectId)) {
        reject(new Error('Token not issued for this application'));
        return;
    }
}
```

### After
```javascript
// Security check: Ensure Firebase is properly configured
if (!this.projectId) {
    throw new Error('Firebase not configured - cannot verify token');
}

// ...

if (tokenInfo.aud !== this.projectId) {
    reject(new Error('Token not issued for this application'));
    return;
}
```

